-- 26 U.S.C. section 121 (exclusion of gain from sale of principal residence).
-- LAYER 1, module 1: the nouns. Types only: no rules, no #EVAL.
-- Every other layer-1 module imports this one.
--
-- The section's own words are quoted, with line numbers of usc26-s121.txt, in the module that encodes each provision.
-- Here a quotation appears only where a type is a table of the text's own list.
--
-- Time is carried as DATE spans: a Span runs from its first day to its last day, both days counted.
-- That counting is the encoder's choice, recorded in NOTES.md (fork F5).
-- A "principal residence", "the gain", "the date of the sale or exchange" and the other terms the section borrows are not typed here:
-- they are facts the person states (the Encoding Guide, section 4).

§ `Nouns of section 121`

-- A stretch of calendar days, both ends counted.
DECLARE Span HAS
    `first day` IS A DATE
    `last day`  IS A DATE

-- One individual's history with the property: when they owned it, and when they used it as their principal residence.
DECLARE Holding HAS
    `periods of ownership`                  IS A LIST OF Span
    `periods of use as the principal residence` IS A LIST OF Span

-- (d)(3)(C): the kinds of paper that make an instrument a "divorce or separation instrument".
-- Four yes/no facts, from which (i), (ii) and (iii) are worked out.
DECLARE Instrument HAS
    `a decree of divorce or separate maintenance`            IS A BOOLEAN
    `a written instrument incident to such a decree`         IS A BOOLEAN
    `a written separation agreement`                         IS A BOOLEAN
    `a decree requiring a spouse to make payments for the support or maintenance of the other spouse` IS A BOOLEAN

-- (d)(3)(B): a period during which a spouse or former spouse is granted use of the property, and by what instrument.
DECLARE `Use granted` HAS
    `days`       IS A Span
    `instrument` IS AN Instrument

-- (d)(7): a stay in a facility.
DECLARE `Stay in a facility` HAS
    `days` IS A Span
    `facility licensed by a State or political subdivision to care for an individual in the taxpayer's condition` IS A BOOLEAN

-- (d)(6): a depreciation adjustment (as section 1250(b)(3) defines it, which is not among the sources) and the period it is attributable to.
DECLARE `Depreciation adjustment` HAS
    `amount`                      IS A NUMBER
    `period it is attributable to` IS A Span

-- (d)(5)(A): the events the text treats as a sale.
DECLARE `Event in respect of the property` IS ONE OF
    `destruction`
    `theft`
    `seizure`
    `requisition`
    `condemnation`
    `sale or exchange`
    `some other event`

-- (d)(9)(A), (d)(12)(A): the capacity in which a person serves.
DECLARE `Capacity of service` IS ONE OF
    `member of the uniformed services`
    `member of the Foreign Service of the United States`
    `employee of the intelligence community`
    `employee of the Peace Corps`
    `enrolled volunteer or volunteer leader under the Peace Corps Act`
    `some other capacity`

-- (d)(9)(C)(iv): the offices named in the text, (I) to (X); (VIII) names eight elements, listed one by one.
DECLARE `Office of the intelligence community` IS ONE OF
    `the Office of the Director of National Intelligence`
    `the Central Intelligence Agency`
    `the National Security Agency`
    `the Defense Intelligence Agency`
    `the National Geospatial-Intelligence Agency`
    `the National Reconnaissance Office`
    `another office within the Department of Defense for the collection of specialized national intelligence through reconnaissance programs`
    `an intelligence element of the Army`
    `an intelligence element of the Navy`
    `an intelligence element of the Air Force`
    `an intelligence element of the Marine Corps`
    `an intelligence element of the Federal Bureau of Investigation`
    `an intelligence element of the Department of Treasury`
    `an intelligence element of the Department of Energy`
    `an intelligence element of the Coast Guard`
    `the Bureau of Intelligence and Research of the Department of State`
    `an element of the Department of Homeland Security concerned with the analyses of foreign intelligence information`
    `some other office`

-- (d)(9), (d)(12): one period of service, and the facts the definitions in (d)(9)(C) ask about.
DECLARE `Period of service` HAS
    `days`                                          IS A Span
    `capacity`                                      IS A `Capacity of service`
    `serving outside the United States`             IS A BOOLEAN
    `miles from the duty station to the property`   IS A NUMBER
    `residing under Government orders in Government quarters` IS A BOOLEAN
    `on active duty pursuant to a call or order`    IS A BOOLEAN
    `days the call or order is for`                 IS A NUMBER
    `the call or order is for an indefinite period` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a member of the uniformed services under section 101(a)(5) of title 10` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a member of the Service under section 103(1) to (5) of the Foreign Service Act of 1980` IS A BOOLEAN
    `an employee as defined by section 2105 of title 5` IS A BOOLEAN
    `office of the intelligence community`          IS AN `Office of the intelligence community`
    `an enrolled volunteer under section 5 of the Peace Corps Act`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `a volunteer leader under section 6 of the Peace Corps Act`     IS A BOOLEAN

-- (b)(5)(C)(ii)(III): a period of temporary absence and the reason given for it.
DECLARE `Temporary absence` HAS
    `days`                                       IS A Span
    `change of employment`                       IS A BOOLEAN
    `health conditions`                          IS A BOOLEAN
    `unforeseen circumstances as may be specified by the Secretary` IS A BOOLEAN
